Imagine there is a giant group of people whose job is to make the rules for a really, really big country called China. 

You know how your school has rules, like raising your hand to speak or taking turns on the slide? Well, countries need rules too, so everyone can be safe and happy. 

In China, this giant group of rule-makers is called the **National People’s Congress** (or NPC for short, which is a bit of a mouthful!). 

Here is what they do:

* **The Big Rule Makers:** Just like the people at your town hall make rules for London, the NPC makes the big rules for all the millions of people living in China. 
* **The Choosers:** They also get to pick the people who will be the "bosses" or leaders of the country to make sure everything runs smoothly. 
* **The Money Checkers:** They look after the country's giant piggy bank to decide how much money should be spent on things like schools, hospitals, and parks.

Think of them like a giant School Council, but instead of just helping your school, they are helping more than a billion people! Every year, they travel to a big meeting in Beijing (the capital city of China) to talk, vote, and decide on the best rules to keep their country running. [end of text]


